I've been playing Nethack for over 14 years, and the number of hit
points I feel the need for has steadily increased. I used to get away
with under 200HP for an ascension, now I don't feel comfortable with
fewer than 300. Especially as I've recently won more games without
wearing an amulet of life saving, having survived all of my eight
ascensions thus far on NAO without consuming one (http://alt.org/
nethack/player.php?player=funcrunch - Wizard ascension didn't make
high score list thus not shown here) - I like having that extra margin
of safety to not even have to look at my HP on the ascension run.

But my latest Cavewoman didn't want to leave any kinds of potions of
healing behind, alchemizing and quaffing all to a max of over 600HP,
which seemed a bit ridiculous. I know, some players have gotten
millions of HP in long games through polyself bug abuse or whatever,
but that's not my goal or interest. Am I wasting my time gaining so
many HP? Not that I'm going for a speed ascension, but could always
stand to be more efficient. Blessed potions of full healing are
quicker and more reliable than nurses/foocubi, but do involve carrying
extra inventory around while collecting sufficient gain energy and
holy water. Alchemy didn't exist yet during my earliest ascensions,
but then some aspects of the game have certainly gotten harder since
then...



